0372 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510372 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-2{x}^{2}+4$ defined on $[-3,3).$  Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension of $G(x)=-4x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+4∼-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{72(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-4x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510372 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1d451e41-c662-5263-b3f7-8483ecaa8976" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510372 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3$ and we are already given the coefficients ${a}_{0}$ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{72(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-3,3),$\n\n- continuous on $[-3,3),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-3)=F(3),$ if we extend the value at $x=3$ using the formula $F(x)=-2{x}^{2}+4.$\n\nTherefore, the $6$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{continuous}$ and $\\text{piecewise smooth}$ on $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{2}+4) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2)+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{72(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\ -4x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{72(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\ -4x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-24(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\ -4x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510492 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186510498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510492 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "352caae4-676a-57d5-bd9d-c7587793e13c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510492 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186510372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510498 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186510561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510498 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "410fa0b4-3fcf-58af-9022-5120be85b47f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510498 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186317373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510561 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f22acf91-843d-568d-9445-425b3e5be0ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510561 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186317374 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
